---
const pageTitle = "See My Eyes – Blind Pixels Studio";
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{pageTitle}</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="See My Eyes is an educational iOS app that simulates real eye conditions using your live camera feed — all processed entirely on-device."
    />
  </head>

  <body class="page">
    <main class="detail layout" aria-labelledby="see-my-eyes-heading">
      <a class="detail__back" href="/">← Back to Blind Pixels Studio</a>

      <header class="detail__header">
        <p class="detail__eyebrow">App</p>
        <h1 id="see-my-eyes-heading">See My Eyes</h1>
        <p class="detail__lede">
          See My Eyes is an educational iOS app that simulates how different
          eye conditions affect vision, using your live camera feed, processed
          entirely on-device.
        </p>
      </header>

      <section class="detail__section">
        <h2>Who it's for</h2>
        <p>
          See My Eyes is for anyone who wants to help others understand what
          living with a visual impairment is like. It’s especially useful for:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>People with low vision wanting to show friends and family how they see</li>
          <li>Educators teaching about vision conditions and accessibility</li>
          <li>Parents, clinicians, and advocates demonstrating visual changes</li>
          <li>Designers or developers evaluating accessibility challenges</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="detail__section">
        <h2>What it does</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Simulates common visual impairments such as RP, macular degeneration, glaucoma, and cataracts</li>
          <li>Processes every camera frame locally; no images ever leave the device</li>
          <li>Lets you adjust intensity to match real-world experiences</li>
          <li>Provides preset profiles for quick demonstration</li>
          <li>Works in real-time using the device’s live camera feed</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="detail__section">
        <h2>Get the app</h2>
        <p>
          Currently in Beta Testing.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>

  <style lang="css">
    body.page {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: "Inter", "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
      background: radial-gradient(circle at top left, #14213d 0%, #07090f 60%);
      color: #f9fafb;
    }

    .layout {
      width: min(960px, 100% - 3rem);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 3.5rem 0 4rem;
    }

    .detail__back {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
      color: #bfdbfe;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }

    .detail__back:hover,
    .detail__back:focus {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .detail__header h1 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem);
    }

    .detail__eyebrow {
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      color: rgba(191, 219, 254, 0.8);
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .detail__lede {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      color: rgba(226, 232, 255, 0.86);
    }

    .detail__section {
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
    }

    .detail__section h2 {
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
      font-size: 1.3rem;
    }

    .detail__section p,
    .detail__section li {
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: rgba(226, 232, 255, 0.9);
    }

    .detail__section ul {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1.2rem;
    }
  </style>
</html>
